  "raw": " assist in understanding the nature of the pathogen. This is so because even with a molecular biological method, difficulty may develop with obtaining sufficient detail to accurately identify all the proteins involved or the complete cellular closure of Herpes Simplex Virus 'Life Warrant' protein resulting from release from destruction cells by possibility and less efficient phagocytosis.\nHerpes Simplex virus is a single-stranded RNA viruses endemic throughout the animal kingdom in many species (1). It is known that there are several different genotypes. In particular more than 100 types have been implicated in human herpesviral infections (2) and many other kinds exist in animals resembling human infection. Although it is present wherever there exists human infection, particularly lanid primate distribution, repetitive recombination has occurred over time to produce different strains exhibiting similar symptoms characteristically characterized as \"cold sores\". Historically, viral conjunctivitis was obtained using isolate growing in 293 cells cultured on fibroblaststimulant serum; however,",
